00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:37.880
On their first day in the forest,

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:40.900
Ronja and Birk worked tirelessly.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.780
The day passed in the blink of an eye.

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:52.220
That night, thoughts of Mattis' Castle filled Ronja's heart with sadness.

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:57.980
In her dream, Mattis was sitting alone in the middle of a pitch black wood,

00:01:57.980 --> 00:01:59.980
sobbing uncontrollably.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:07.420
The Lost Knife

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:07.420
The Lost Knife

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:35.640
We have to haul in the fish before the cuckoo calls!

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:50.900
<i>If</i> there are any fish to haul in.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:57.150
I suppose you expect the net to be full?

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:03.400
There are salmon in this river!

00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:09.510
I'll be shocked if we didn't catch a single one!

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:19.490
<i>I'll</i> be shocked if you don't fall head-first into the river, the way you're frolic around.

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:32.600
This is my spring frolic!

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:35.350
Spring frolic, huh?

00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:47.010
Looks like path was made just for spring frolics.

00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:49.870
Who do you think cleared it to begin with?

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:52.870
It was probably Mattis!

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:57.460
Maybe when he was staying in the Bear's Cave!

00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:00.340
He likes salmon.

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:03.320
He always has.

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:05.730
That's why...

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:09.970
Ronja!

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:44.610
My sister!

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:47.210
Now you're not going to die of hunger.

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:49.000
I promise you that.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:53.170
Not until winter, at least.

00:04:53.170 --> 00:04:54.070
Uh-huh?

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:01.640
Though winter's too far off to worry about that now.

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:10.200
Birk, your foot!

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:15.480
I nicked myself with the axe when I was trimming the branches off that log.

00:05:17.090 --> 00:05:23.040
With a little cut like this, you should just let it stop bleeding on its own.

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:25.430
Don't act so carefree about stuff like this.

00:05:25.430 --> 00:05:29.260
Bears might catch the scent of blood and come after us.

00:05:32.590 --> 00:05:36.060
Then I'd just show who's boss with my spear.

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:38.740
My mother would...

00:05:41.010 --> 00:05:45.940
My mother would usually put dry moss on a fresh wound.

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:51.570
I really should gather up some moss for us.

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:56.490
I mean, who knows when you'll cut yourself again?

00:05:59.510 --> 00:06:02.290
You might just be right about that.

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:37.600
After three days, Ronja finally asked Birk:

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:42.770
Birk, which do you think is worse?

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:47.680
Having only grilled salmon to eat day in and day out,

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:50.240
or getting blisters on your hands?

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:56.270
They're both pretty bad.

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:01.270
Here.

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:08.740
But I know this much:

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:13.300
We should have brought something to use as a chisel.

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:17.240
Carving out a bowl with just a knife is nearly impossible.

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:25.640
Now, I just have to carve a little more out of this.

00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:27.340
Hand over the knife.

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:31.040
Knife?

00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:33.320
You have it, don't you?

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:37.500
No, you used it last.

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:39.320
Fork it over!

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:44.330
I don't have the knife.

00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:49.000
Didn't you didn't hear me the first time?!

00:08:50.370 --> 00:08:52.590
What have you done with it then?

00:08:56.050 --> 00:09:00.140
Seriously?! What have <i>I</i> done with it?

00:09:03.720 --> 00:09:07.080
<i>You</i> were the one who had it last!

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:10.320
That's a lie!

00:09:12.930 --> 00:09:18.740
Didn't I tell you that we needed that knife to survive?!

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:26.500
Then you should have kept track of it better!

00:09:29.010 --> 00:09:32.090
You good-for-nothing!

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:36.290
You just screw things up and then blame someone else!

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:44.620
I see how it is.

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:49.300
Back to your old ways I see,

00:09:49.300 --> 00:09:50.810
robber's daughter.

00:09:53.930 --> 00:09:56.600
You haven't changed at all.

00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:58.100
I get it now.

00:09:59.690 --> 00:10:03.360
How am I supposed to live with you?

00:10:04.060 --> 00:10:07.480
Nobody's making you, Borka robber!

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:11.260
I hope you enjoy living alone with your precious knife!

00:10:11.260 --> 00:10:13.360
If you can find it, that is!

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:20.320
I hope Hell's Gap swallows you!

00:10:30.130 --> 00:10:32.850
May the harpies take you!

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:36.860
You'll be quite at home with them!

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:51.910
<i>I really should gather up some moss for us.</i>

00:10:51.910 --> 00:10:56.470
<i>I mean, who knows when you'll cut yourself again?</i>

00:10:57.250 --> 00:10:59.970
Screw this!

00:11:16.390 --> 00:11:20.430
Ronja, the Robber's Daughter

00:11:16.390 --> 00:11:20.430
Ronja, the Robber's Daughter

00:11:36.650 --> 00:11:39.750
<i>I hope you enjoy living alone with your precious knife!</i>

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:43.610
Where are you going to stay then?

00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:49.330
Whatever. You can stay wherever the hell you want.

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:53.600
I won't let her in here again, even if she comes crawling back.

00:11:58.200 --> 00:12:03.140
She'll be back soon enough, begging me to let her in, and I'll just say:

00:12:05.180 --> 00:12:08.750
You should've come back sooner.

00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:11.100
It's too late now.

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:32.060
She didn't leave because of me...

00:13:44.910 --> 00:13:47.870
<i>Yes, I'm coming!</i>

00:13:49.400 --> 00:13:50.380
<i>Don't!</i>

00:13:53.980 --> 00:13:55.510
<i>Let me go!</i>

00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:01.540
<i>Then who are you?</i>

00:14:02.830 --> 00:14:05.330
<i>Did the fox... bite you?</i>

00:14:05.330 --> 00:14:07.540
<i>Don't leave me!</i>

00:14:07.540 --> 00:14:09.920
<i>Don't ever leave me again, okay?!</i>

00:14:09.920 --> 00:14:11.820
<i>Things are different now!</i>

00:14:11.820 --> 00:14:14.100
<i>Now, I have a brother!</i>

00:14:48.010 --> 00:14:51.180
Ronja!

00:14:57.100 --> 00:14:59.980
Ronja!

00:15:05.410 --> 00:15:08.070
Ronja!

00:15:08.680 --> 00:15:12.520
Ronja!

00:15:43.980 --> 00:15:50.020
I knew from the start how badly she missed Mattis.

00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:07.780
Poor thing.

00:16:15.610 --> 00:16:16.860
Birk!

00:16:18.170 --> 00:16:19.420
Ronja!

00:16:20.530 --> 00:16:22.330
Did you see that bear?!

00:16:22.940 --> 00:16:25.580
That bear took her foal!

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:28.020
He killed it!

00:16:44.650 --> 00:16:47.170
Ronja, remember...

00:16:47.170 --> 00:16:48.850
Whenever you're injured...

00:16:50.620 --> 00:16:52.070
Moss!

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:53.610
Go get some!

00:16:53.970 --> 00:16:55.390
But...

00:16:55.390 --> 00:17:00.620
But I can't leave you here alone when that bear might still be around!

00:17:01.060 --> 00:17:02.590
Hurry up and go!

00:17:08.020 --> 00:17:10.650
I need to stay with her.

00:17:11.400 --> 00:17:15.010
She needs someone to comfort her.

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:20.750
Got it? Get going already!

00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:23.270
O-Okay!

00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:52.760
Wuffor they be doing that?

00:17:53.290 --> 00:17:56.830
Wuffor they be doing that?

00:17:59.610 --> 00:18:00.840
Oh, look!

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:02.960
Rumphobs!

00:18:06.770 --> 00:18:11.480
As long as you guys are around, nothing dangerous will come this way.

00:18:12.950 --> 00:18:15.740
The horse isn't scared any more either.

00:18:18.770 --> 00:18:21.420
Wuffor those two be laughing?

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:25.030
Wuffor those two be laughing?

00:19:30.380 --> 00:19:31.910
The bleeding's stopped!

00:19:32.930 --> 00:19:34.900
The moss dried up, too.

00:19:39.880 --> 00:19:44.100
Drink up. The water will replenish your fluids.

00:19:47.400 --> 00:19:50.890
Let's keep her tied up near this spring until she's healed.

00:19:51.640 --> 00:19:54.370
Bears don't come around here.

00:19:55.410 --> 00:19:57.870
Don't grieve so deeply.

00:19:57.870 --> 00:20:01.640
When spring comes around again, you can have another foal.

00:20:06.610 --> 00:20:11.890
That milk was for your foal, wasn't it?

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:15.490
Why not let us have it instead?

00:20:18.840 --> 00:20:22.080
She's our horse. We should name her.

00:20:22.080 --> 00:20:24.150
What should we call her?

00:20:25.780 --> 00:20:26.810
Lia.

00:20:28.600 --> 00:20:31.850
I think we should call her Lia.

00:20:31.850 --> 00:20:36.330
Mattis had a mare when he was little, and that was her name.

00:20:36.850 --> 00:20:38.240
Lia, huh?

00:20:38.860 --> 00:20:40.460
Sounds good to me.

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:46.040
Lia.

00:21:14.570 --> 00:21:18.610
It's a shame that we lost the knife.

00:21:38.140 --> 00:21:41.050
Fortunately, it turned up again.

00:21:43.130 --> 00:21:46.280
It was just under the moss,

00:21:46.280 --> 00:21:50.820
hiding out while we squabbled with each other.

00:21:57.860 --> 00:22:03.030
Do you know what I've been thinking?

00:22:06.760 --> 00:22:13.930
I've been thinking about how easily everything can be ruined...

00:22:14.520 --> 00:22:16.470
For no reason at all.

00:22:17.210 --> 00:22:22.520
Let's take care to prevent something like that from happening again.

00:22:24.680 --> 00:22:30.070
Do you know what <i>I've</i> been thinking?

00:22:37.400 --> 00:22:43.830
I've been thinking, you're more important to me than a thousand knives!

00:22:47.490 --> 00:22:52.340
Now you just sound foolish.

00:23:00.630 --> 00:23:05.730
That was something Lovis occasionally said to Mattis.

00:23:07.080 --> 00:23:13.190
Ronja and Birk kept on laughing and laughing.

